<Sequential id="uk_05">

  <Vertical id="uk_05_s1" title="A name above the pavement">
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s1_text">
The bus had left a stripe of dirty water up Zofia's tights. She rubbed it with a tissue until the tissue came apart, then stood beneath the blue plaque at 12 St James's Square with white shreds stuck to her knee.

Morwenna held the folder under her coat, tucking back its cracked corner.

Above them was Ada's name. Below it, on Morwenna's phone, was a different account of her work: a caption from the Witness Workshop. They had brought that one themselves. It wasn't part of the building.

Zofia looked from the phone to the woman beside the wall. A passing man walked between them without slowing down. Morwenna watched Zofia instead.

The woman looked at the folder, then at the tissue disintegrating in Zofia's hand.

Zofia had practised an introduction on the bus. It began with the petition and ended with the date they were running out of time. Now she couldn't remember the middle.

She pocketed the tissue. She wasn't asking a dead mathematician to wait while she found a bin.
    </Markdown>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="uk_05_s2" title="The missing author">
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s2_intro">Beneath the plaque, Morwenna shields the phone from the rain.</Markdown>
    <Chat id="uk_05_missing_author" src="charter.chatpeg" clip="missing_author"/>
  </Vertical>
  <!--AddFlashcardActions deck="ojaj-uk" cards="ada-life ada-babbage ada-notes ada-vision"-->

  <Vertical id="uk_05_s3" title="The room they had booked">
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s3_text">
The study room smelled of damp coats and hot printer paper. Someone had left a strip of blue tack stuck to the table. Ollie stretched it between his fingers until Grace put the folder on top of it.

Their escort checked the booking, pointed out where they were to wait afterwards, and sat by the door. Morwenna put the return time face up beside her pencil case. Nobody could pretend not to have seen it.

The radiator clicked. Zofia kept her coat on. Ada was only a voice now, carried from the square at Zofia's invitation. Hale had come too, objecting before they reached the table.

The petition lay in the middle, underneath everybody's elbows. It had a title and room for living signatures. It did not yet have a first sentence that survived Hale reading it.

Morwenna laid out the Charter extracts. One agreed paragraph before the booking ended, and Grace could take it for signatures. Otherwise: another afternoon on “require”.

Zofia uncapped her pen with her teeth. Grace held out a hand for the cap.
    </Markdown>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="uk_05_s4" title="Forty days">
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s4_intro">At the study-room table, Hale starts again before Zofia can write.</Markdown>
    <Chat id="uk_05_forty_days" src="charter.chatpeg" clip="forty_days"/>
  </Vertical>
