  <Vertical id="uk_05_s7" title="What can go in the attachment?">
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s7_intro">
Grace stood beside the study-room door with her bag on. Her bus was due. Morwenna slid the attachment over for a last look before Grace signed it.

Zofia's heading read **Two independent witnesses**. Under Will's name she had put **Hubert hanged, 27 October 1666**.

She drew a line on the back:

**September 1666: Will dies → 27 October: Hubert is hanged → today: Zofia tells Will.**

The pen stopped. She had heard him repeat it. She had counted that as another source.

“Sign now?” Grace asked. “Or am I going?”
    </Markdown>
    <CapaProblem id="uk_05_choice" title="What does Zofia do?" maxAttempts="1" showanswer="never">
      <CorrectGrader id="uk_05_choice_grader">
        <Markdown id="uk_05_choice_prompt">**What does Zofia do?**</Markdown>
        <ChoiceInput id="uk_05_choice_input">
          <Key id="uk_05_choice_a" value="a">A. Cross out “independent” and separate what Will remembers from what she told him. Ask Grace to wait for the corrected sheet.</Key>
          <Key id="uk_05_choice_b" value="b">B. Get Grace's signature now. Will knows about Hubert now; fix the heading after Grace catches her bus.</Key>
        </ChoiceInput>
        <Explanation id="uk_05_choice_explanation" showWhen="answered">
          <Markdown id="uk_05_choice_explanation_text">
Will remembers a delivery being weighed, not deliberate fire-setting. He died in September 1666, before Hubert's execution on 27 October. Hubert's confession was false; later evidence placed him at sea when the Fire began, arriving two days afterwards. Zofia has told Will this. His repeating it supplies no independent confirmation. Doyle likewise believed the Cottingley photographs at his death in 1930; Zofia's later update that they were fakes cannot become his original memory. Both updates must be labelled as coming through her.
          </Markdown>
        </Explanation>
      </CorrectGrader>
    </CapaProblem>
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s7_after_a" when="@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission ? (@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission).includes('a') : false">
Zofia rewrites the dates. Grace watches the clock, then shoulders her bag. “Send me the finished one.” She leaves without signing. Under the later evidence Zofia puts her own name: she supplied it. There is one fewer signature today.
    </Markdown>
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s7_after_b" when="@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission ? (@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission).includes('b') : false">
Grace signs and runs. Morwenna reads the heading before clipping on the sheet. “This isn't the account I thought she was signing.” She sets it aside and asks Zofia to date each statement. The escort calls time before they finish. They must leave the table and complete the correction outside; Grace will have to see the corrected version before her signature can accompany it.
    </Markdown>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="uk_05_s8" title="A request we can sign" when="@uk_05_choice.correct === correctness.correct">
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s8_intro_a" when="@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission ? (@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission).includes('a') : false">At the study-room table, Zofia moves the unsigned copy away from Grace's empty chair.</Markdown>
    <Markdown id="uk_05_s8_intro_b" when="@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission ? (@uk_05_choice_grader.lastSubmission).includes('b') : false">In the waiting corridor, Zofia balances the corrected attachment on the folder while Morwenna checks it.</Markdown>
    <Chat id="uk_05_request_we_can_sign" src="charter.chatpeg" clip="request_we_can_sign"/>
  </Vertical>

